<title>ITALY: Specialists bid for 369 bln lire of Italy Btps.</title>
<headline>Specialists bid for 369 bln lire of Italy Btps.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Specialist bond traders bid for 369 billion lire of 10-year fixed-rate bonds (BTP) against the Italian Treasury's offer of 400 billion lire of paper.</p>
<p>Earlier, the Treasury received bids for 5.97 trillion lire at the open auction for the November 1, 2006 paper, against 4.0 trillion lire worth of paper on offer.</p>
<p>The auction price was set at 102.80 from 103.70 at the previous 10-year Btp sale on December 17.</p>
